Description: Replace distutils with setuptools in setup.py.in
 Python 3.12 removed the distutils module from the standard library
 (PEP 632). The gpgme Python bindings still import from distutils.core
 and distutils.command.build, which fails on Python 3.12:
 .
   ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'distutils'
 .
 Replace the distutils imports with their setuptools equivalents.
 setuptools provides drop-in replacements for both distutils.core
 (setup, Extension) and distutils.command.build (build).  The build
 dependency python3-setuptools is already pulled in transitively via
 dh-python, and is now also declared explicitly in Build-Depends.
Author: st0nie <st0nie@users.noreply.github.com>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1039724
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-07-06

--- a/lang/python/setup.py.in
+++ b/lang/python/setup.py.in
@@ -18,8 +18,8 @@
 #    License along with this library; if not, write to the Free Software
 #    Foundation, Inc., 59 Temple Place, Suite 330, Boston, MA 02111-1307  USA
 
-from distutils.core import setup, Extension
-from distutils.command.build import build
+from setuptools import setup, Extension
+from setuptools.command.build import build
 
 import glob
 import os
